1:["$","$Ld",null,{"page":{"id":"library--what-is-a-word","kind":"library-article","route":"/roadmap/library/what-is-a-word","sourceUrl":"https://refold.la/roadmap/library/what-is-a-word","sourceHash":"098da74108038d8f838f50fb6367c95af64181629b6006e549cd1f5a7cd7b653","collectedAt":"2026-09-01T23:11:25.731Z","bodyMode":"authorized-full-body","title":{"en":"What is a Word","zh":"什么是词"},"description":{"en":"","zh":""},"segments":[{"id":"segment-0001","type":"blockquote","content":{"en":"<p>“What’s in a name? That which we call a rose by any other name would smell as sweet.” - Juliet, Act II, Scene II</p>","zh":"<p>“名字里有什么？玫瑰即使换个名字，闻起来依然芬芳。”——朱丽叶，第二幕第二场</p>"}},{"id":"segment-0003","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"That's a great question Juliet! What <em>is</em> a name? Or word for that matter?","zh":"这是个很棒的问题，朱丽叶！什么<em>是</em>名字？或者说，什么才算一个词？"}},{"id":"segment-0004","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"This question is surprisingly difficult to answer for a linguist. There <strong>is</strong> no single, agreed-upon definition of a word. Every attempt to define what a word is has so many exceptions that it can't possibly be accepted even as a \"good enough\" definition.","zh":"对于语言学家来说，这个问题出人意料地难以回答。没有一个统一且公认的“词”的定义。每一种定义“词”的尝试都有太多例外，以至于连“足够好”的定义都算不上。"}},{"id":"segment-0005","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"But despite that, we use the word \"word\" very often, without much difficulty.","zh":"但即便如此，我们仍然经常使用“词”这个词，而且并不会遇到太大困难。"}},{"id":"segment-0006","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"In everyday life, the exact definition of what a word is doesn't bother us. It's not super relevant to getting our point across:","zh":"在日常生活中，我们并不在意一个词的精确定义。它与表达清楚自己的意思并没有太大关系："}},{"id":"segment-0007","type":"blockquote","content":{"en":"<p>\"Mother fu----\" \"HEY! Don't say that word in this house!\" \"But MOM, what even <em>is</em> a word?\"</p>","zh":"<p>“他妈的——”“嘿！不许在这个家里说那个词！”“可是妈妈，到底什么<em>是</em>词啊？”</p>"}},{"id":"segment-0009","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"However, if you're writing a complete guide to learning a foreign language, you're going to end up using the word \"word\" quite a lot. So having an agreed upon definition, even if rough, helps clear things up.","zh":"然而，如果你要写一份完整的外语学习指南，就会经常用到“词”这个词。因此，即使只是一个粗略的共识性定义，也有助于把事情说清楚。"}},{"id":"word-families","type":"heading","level":2,"content":{"en":"Word Families","zh":"词族"}},{"id":"segment-0011","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"When we talk about learning words in a foreign language, we're not talking about every single different combination of letters.","zh":"当我们谈论学习一门外语中的词时，并不是在说每一种不同的字母组合。"}},{"id":"segment-0012","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"By that logic, these would all be different words:","zh":"按照那种逻辑，下面这些都应该算不同的词："}},{"id":"segment-0013","type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"en":"Eat","zh":"吃"},{"en":"Eats","zh":"吃（第三人称单数）"},{"en":"To eat","zh":"吃（不定式）"},{"en":"Ate","zh":"吃了"},{"en":"Eaten","zh":"吃过"},{"en":"Eatery","zh":"餐馆"},{"en":"Eater","zh":"食客"},{"en":"etc.","zh":"等等"}]},{"id":"segment-0014","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"And the word \"man\" would be considered one word, even with two very different meanings:","zh":"而“man”这个词即使有两个截然不同的含义，也会被视为一个词："}},{"id":"segment-0015","type":"blockquote","content":{"en":"<p>The man mans the boat.</p>","zh":"<p>The man mans the boat.</p>"}},{"id":"segment-0017","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"So instead we count word families, which are groups of semantically related words.","zh":"所以，我们会计算词族，也就是语义相关的一组词。"}},{"id":"segment-0018","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"Eat, eats, ate, eating, eater, eaten, etc. is a single word family and so is good, better, best.","zh":"Eat、eats、ate、eating、eater、eaten 等属于同一个词族，good、better、best 也属于同一个词族。"}}],"cards":[]},"siteBasePath":"/my_learning_docs"}]
